izes Cortactin and remodels Arp2/3-containing actin branches in lamellipodia</article-title><source>Cell</source><comment>in press</comment><year>2008</year></element-citation></ref><ref id="R30"><label>30</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gallo</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Cante-Barrett</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Crabtree</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lymphocyte calcium signaling from membrane to nucleus</article-title><source>Nat Immunol</source><volume>7</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>32</lpage><year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16357855</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R31"><label>31</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Puck</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Candotti</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lessons from the Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><volume>355</volume><fpage>1759</fpage><lpage>1761</lpage><year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17065636</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R32"><label>32</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fischer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human primary immunodeficiency diseases</article-title><source>Immunity</source><volume>27</volume><fpage>835</fpage><lpage>845</lpage><year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18093537</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R33"><label>33</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buckley</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The multiple causes of human SCID</article-title><source>J Clin Inve